message:
[params] Fix issue #359

* Added two free functions, apply() and foreach().

    /// Pick parameter by name and apply a generic functor f to it.
    template <typename F> void apply(const params& opts, const std::string& optname, F const& f);

    /// Apply a generic functor f to each defined parameter
    template <typename F> void foreach(const params& opts, F const& f);

    For any allowed parameter type T, f must be callable as
    f(const std::string& name, boost::optional<T> const& val, boost::optional<T> const& defval, const std::string& descr)

* Added new method option_description_type::is_trigger().
* Added a unit-test for the new functions.

Introduced explicit alps::params cast.

Like this:
std::string s=p["file"].as<std::string>()+".out";

ALEA: stream_serializer, a result serialization plugin

This plugin should allow for Boost/HPX serialization of *_result<T> types.
To enable the plugin for all supported ALEA result types in an HPX application
one must include alps/alea/plugin/stream_serializer.hpp as follows,

    #include <hpx/runtime/serialization/serialize.hpp>
    #include <hpx/runtime/serialization/complex.hpp>

    #include <alps/alea/plugin/stream_serializer.hpp>

    namespace alps { namespace alea {
    HPX_SERIALIZATION_SPLIT_FREE_TEMPLATE((template <typename T>), (mean_result<T>));
    HPX_SERIALIZATION_SPLIT_FREE_TEMPLATE((template <typename T>), (var_result<T,circular_var>));
    HPX_SERIALIZATION_SPLIT_FREE_TEMPLATE((template <typename T>), (var_result<T,elliptic_var>));
    HPX_SERIALIZATION_SPLIT_FREE_TEMPLATE((template <typename T>), (cov_result<T,circular_var>));
    HPX_SERIALIZATION_SPLIT_FREE_TEMPLATE((template <typename T>), (cov_result<T,elliptic_var>));
    HPX_SERIALIZATION_SPLIT_FREE_TEMPLATE((template <typename T>), (autocorr_result<T>));
    HPX_SERIALIZATION_SPLIT_FREE_TEMPLATE((template <typename T>), (batch_result<T>));
    }}

Direct access to autocorrelation of named accumulators.

Not yet complete: no direct access to autocorrelation of the results.
Aso, the test is not testing the validity of the autocorrelation.

Usage:
```C++

  typedef alps::accumulators::FullBinningAccumulator<double> accumulator_type;
  accumulator_type acc("my_acc");
  // ....

  accumulator_type::autocorrelation_type my_acc_tau=acc.tau(); // autocorrelation
```

fixed many compiler warnings
if the following flags are added to CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS the output of clang gets rid of some garbage:
-Wall -Wno-unknown-pragmas -Wno-unused-function -Wno-overloaded-virtual -Wno-unneeded-internal-declaration -Wno-unused-variable -Wno-return-type-c-linkage

Ability to have NoBinningAccumulator<custom_type>.

It is assumed that `custom_type` is mathematically sane. Namely:
```C++

typedef alps::numeric::scalar<custom_type> scalar_type;
custom_type x,y;
scalar_type s;

assert(s*x == x*s);
assert(s+x == x+s);
assert(s-x == -x+s);
assert(s*x*y == x*y*s);
assert(pow(x,scalar_type(1./3.)) == cbrt(x));
```

[params] Fix issue #359 (#360)

* Added two free functions, apply() and foreach().

    /// Pick parameter by name and apply a generic functor f to it.
    template <typename F> void apply(const params& opts, const std::string& optname, F const& f);

    /// Apply a generic functor f to each defined parameter
    template <typename F> void foreach(const params& opts, F const& f);

    For any allowed parameter type T, f must be callable as
    f(const std::string& name, boost::optional<T> const& val, boost::optional<T> const& defval, const std::string& descr)

* Added new method option_description_type::is_trigger().
* Added a unit-test for the new functions.

Implemented cast to Result originated from different Accumulator.

Works this way:

    result_set rset;
    // ....
    const result_wrapper& r1=rset["no_binning"];
    result_wrapper r2=cast<FullBinningAccumulator<double>::result_type,
                           NoBinningAccumulator<double>::result_type>(rset["full_binning"]);
    result_wrapper rsum=r1+r2;

(Fixing issue #210).

Add MPI merge capability for individual named accumulators.

Usage: ```
   FullBinningAccumulator<double> acc;
   boost::mpi::communicator comm;
   // .... collect data ....
   acc.collective_merge(comm,root_rank);
```

Printing of missing arguments is implemented and tested.

Usage:

   if (par.has_missing(std::out)) {
      return 1; /* missing mandatory args */
   }

This closes issue #124 (also mentioned in issue #195).

fixed many compiler warnings
if the following flags are added to CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS the output of clang gets rid of some garbage:
-Wall -Wno-unknown-pragmas -Wno-unused-function -Wno-overloaded-virtual -Wno-unneeded-internal-declaration -Wno-unused-variable -Wno-return-type-c-linkage

Implemented detection of unused arguments

This addresses issue #377. Usage:

Checking for any unused arguments:
```c++
    if (p.has_unused(std::cout)) { // any unused args? print them
       return 1;
    }
```

Checking for unused arguments in a particular section:
```c++
    if (p.has_unused(std::cout, "solver")) { // any unused args in solver section? print them
       return 1;
    }
```

Checking for unused arguments in a top section:
```c++
    if (p.has_unused(std::cout, "")) { // any unused args in top section? print them
       return 1;
    }
```
